IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa21-ch1-panel.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 28, Chapter 1 -- The Takeover Panel (ss 942 to 965).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Written from the text alone (the plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk named in
-- inputs/SOURCES.md, not the official text). Every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29 and the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05; see NOTES.md):
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes to the case;
--   JUST FALSE  the text itself says no to the case in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if", "only if",
--               "unless", "where", a closed list, a flat negative, a period it fixes) -- never merely because it is silent;
--   NOTHING     not covered: silent, a list not closed, "includes", an undefined term, a pointer outside the sources
--               (the Panel's own rules, Schedules 1C and 2, other Acts), or a grant limited by its own wording.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Where a function takes a MAYBE BOOLEAN input named for another section,
-- that is a seam (PLAN.md section 4): the answering part's function is wired to it at the merge.

§ `Part 28, Chapter 1: The Takeover Panel`

§§ `The Panel and its rules (ss 942 to 946)`

-- s 942(1): the body is a term defined by the section.
-- src:13136 | (1) The body known as the Panel on Takeovers and Mergers (“the Panel”) is to have the functions conferred on it by or under this Chapter.
@ref s 942(1) The Panel (src:13136-13136)
GIVEN `the body is known as the Panel on Takeovers and Mergers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 942(1) the body is the Panel` MEANS
    IF `the body is known as the Panel on Takeovers and Mergers`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body known as the Panel on Takeovers and Mergers (“the Panel”)"

-- s 942(2): a power of the Panel; for the person, what the Panel may do about them.
-- src:13137 | (2) The Panel may do anything that it considers necessary or expedient for the purposes of, or in connection with, its functions.
@ref s 942(2) The Panel (src:13137-13137)
GIVEN `the Panel considers the act necessary or expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is for the purposes of, or in connection with, the Panel's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 942(2) the Panel may do the act` MEANS
    IF `the Panel considers the act necessary or expedient` AND `the act is for the purposes of, or in connection with, the Panel's functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to do what the Panel "considers necessary or expedient for the purposes of, or in connection with, its functions"

-- s 943(6) and s 953(8): "Section 1 (meaning of company) does not apply for the purposes of this section."
DECLARE `s 943(6) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 943(6) section 943`
    `s 943(6) another provision`

-- src:13159 | (6) Section 1 (meaning of “company”) does not apply for the purposes of this section.
@ref s 943(6) Rules (src:13159-13159)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 943(6) provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 943(6) section 1 applies for the purposes of the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 943(6) section 943` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 1 (meaning of “company”) does not apply for the purposes of this section."
    WHEN `s 943(6) another provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of section 943

-- s 943(7): "takeover bid" includes a bid within paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C (a seam: Schedule 1C is coa28's).
-- src:13160 | (7) In this section “takeover bid” includes a takeover bid within the meaning given by paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C.
@ref s 943(7) Rules (src:13160-13160)
GIVEN `sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 943(7) the bid is a takeover bid for the purposes of section 943` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“takeover bid” includes a takeover bid within the meaning given by paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the bid is within paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C is that Schedule's answer

-- s 943(9): "A reference to rules in the following provisions of this Chapter is to rules under this section."
-- src:13162 | (9) A reference to rules in the following provisions of this Chapter is to rules under this section.
@ref s 943(9) Rules (src:13162-13162)
GIVEN `the rules are rules under section 943` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 943(9) the reference to rules in the following provisions of Chapter 1 is a reference to the rules` MEANS
    IF `the rules are rules under section 943`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference to rules in the following provisions of this Chapter is to rules under this section."

-- s 944(3): the Panel must make the text of an instrument containing rules public immediately after it is made.
-- src:13171 | (3) Immediately after an instrument containing rules is made, the text must be made available to the public, with or without payment, in whatever way the Panel thinks appropriate.
@ref s 944(3) Further provisions about rules (src:13171-13171)
GIVEN `the text was made available to the public immediately after the instrument was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 944(3) the Panel has made the text available as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the text was made available to the public immediately after the instrument was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Immediately after an instrument containing rules is made, the text must be made available to the public"

-- s 944(4): a person is not taken to have contravened a rule if he shows the text had not been made available.
-- src:13172 | (4) A person is not to be taken to have contravened a rule if he shows that at the time of the alleged contravention the text of the rule had not been made available as required by subsection (3).
@ref s 944(4) Further provisions about rules (src:13172-13172)
GIVEN `the person shows that when the alleged contravention happened the text of the rule had not been made available as subsection (3) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 944(4) the person is protected from being taken to have contravened the rule` MEANS
    IF `the person shows that when the alleged contravention happened the text of the rule had not been made available as subsection (3) requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he shows that at the time of the alleged contravention the text of the rule had not been made available as required by subsection (3)"
    -- this subsection gives no protection on these facts (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)), which is not to say the person has no defence at all

-- s 944(5): the evidential weight of a certified printed copy of an instrument purporting to be made by the Panel.
DECLARE `s 944(5) place of the proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `s 944(5) Scotland`
    `s 944(5) elsewhere in the United Kingdom`

DECLARE `s 944(5) weight of the certified copy` IS ONE OF
    `s 944(5) is evidence`
    `s 944(5) is sufficient evidence`
    `s 944(5) not covered by this subsection`

-- src:13173 | (5) The production of a printed copy of an instrument purporting to be made by the Panel on which is endorsed a certificate signed by an officer of the Panel authorised by it for that purpose and stating—
-- src:13174 | (a) that the instrument was made by the Panel,
-- src:13175 | (b) that the copy is a true copy of the instrument, and
-- src:13176 | (c) that on a specified date the text of the instrument was made available to the public as required by subsection (3),
-- src:13177 | is evidence (or in Scotland sufficient evidence) of the facts stated in the certificate.
@ref s 944(5) Further provisions about rules (src:13173-13177)
GIVEN `a printed copy of an instrument purporting to be made by the Panel is produced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is endorsed with a certificate signed by an officer of the Panel authorised by it for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the instrument was made by the Panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that the copy is a true copy of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states that on a specified date the text was made available to the public as subsection (3) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `s 944(5) place of the proceedings`
GIVETH A `s 944(5) weight of the certified copy`
`s 944(5) the weight of the certified copy` MEANS
    IF       `a printed copy of an instrument purporting to be made by the Panel is produced`
         AND `it is endorsed with a certificate signed by an officer of the Panel authorised by it for that purpose`
         AND `the certificate states that the instrument was made by the Panel`
         AND `the certificate states that the copy is a true copy of the instrument`
         AND `the certificate states that on a specified date the text was made available to the public as subsection (3) requires`
    THEN CONSIDER place
         WHEN `s 944(5) Scotland` THEN `s 944(5) is sufficient evidence`
         WHEN `s 944(5) elsewhere in the United Kingdom` THEN `s 944(5) is evidence`
    ELSE `s 944(5) not covered by this subsection` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for a copy endorsed with a certificate stating (a), (b) and (c)

-- s 944(6): a certificate purporting to be signed as in (5) is treated as properly signed unless the contrary is shown.
-- src:13178 | (6) A certificate purporting to be signed as mentioned in subsection (5) is to be treated as having been properly signed unless the contrary is shown.
@ref s 944(6) Further provisions about rules (src:13178-13178)
GIVEN `the certificate purports to be signed as mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 944(6) the certificate is treated as properly signed` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the certificate purports to be signed as mentioned in subsection (5)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the presumption is for a certificate "purporting to be signed as mentioned in subsection (5)"
    ELSE IF `the contrary is shown`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the contrary is shown"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 944(7): a person who wishes to rely on an instrument in legal proceedings may require the Panel to endorse a copy.
-- src:13179 | (7) A person who wishes in any legal proceedings to rely on an instrument by which rules are made may require the Panel to endorse a copy of the instrument with a certificate of the kind mentioned in subsection (5).
@ref s 944(7) Further provisions about rules (src:13179-13179)
GIVEN `the person wishes in legal proceedings to rely on an instrument by which rules are made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 944(7) the person may require the Panel to endorse a copy of the instrument with a certificate` MEANS
    IF `the person wishes in legal proceedings to rely on an instrument by which rules are made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "a person who wishes in any legal proceedings to rely on an instrument by which rules are made"

-- s 945(1): the Panel may give rulings on the interpretation, application or effect of rules.
-- src:13181 | (1) The Panel may give rulings on the interpretation, application or effect of rules.
@ref s 945(1) Rulings (src:13181-13181)
GIVEN `the ruling is on the interpretation, application or effect of rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 945(1) the Panel may give the ruling` MEANS
    IF `the ruling is on the interpretation, application or effect of rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "rulings on the interpretation, application or effect of rules"

-- s 945(2): to the extent and in the circumstances the rules specify, and subject to any review or appeal, a ruling binds.
-- src:13182 | (2) To the extent and in the circumstances specified in rules, and subject to any review or appeal, a ruling has binding effect.
@ref s 945(2) Rulings (src:13182-13182)
GIVEN `s 943 the rules specify that the ruling has binding effect to this extent and in these circumstances` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a review or appeal of the ruling is pending or has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 945(2) the ruling has binding effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 943 the rules specify that the ruling has binding effect to this extent and in these circumstances`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `a review or appeal of the ruling is pending or has been decided`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the binding effect is "subject to any review or appeal" and the text does not say what a review or appeal does to it
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the ruling binds "to the extent and in the circumstances specified in rules", and outside them the text says nothing
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what the Panel's rules specify is not among the sources

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Information (ss 947 to 949)`

-- s 947(1): the Panel may by notice in writing require a person to produce documents or provide information.
-- src:13190 | (1) The Panel may by notice in writing require a person—
-- src:13191 | (a) to produce any documents that are specified or described in the notice;
-- src:13192 | (b) to provide, in the form and manner specified in the notice, such information as may be specified or described in the notice.
@ref s 947(1) Power to require documents and information (src:13190-13192)
GIVEN `the Panel has required the person by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies or describes the documents, or the information and the form and manner of providing it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(1) the Panel has required the person to produce the documents or provide the information` MEANS
    IF `the Panel has required the person by notice in writing` AND `the notice specifies or describes the documents, or the information and the form and manner of providing it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "by notice in writing" for documents "specified or described in the notice" and information "specified or described in the notice"

-- s 947(2): the day by which a requirement must be complied with is the end of the period the notice specifies.
-- src:13193 | (2) A requirement under subsection (1) must be complied with—
-- src:13194 | (a) at a place specified in the notice, and
-- src:13195 | (b) before the end of such reasonable period as may be so specified.
@ref s 947(2) Power to require documents and information (src:13193-13195)
GIVEN `the day the person complied` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period specified in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the person complied at the place specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(2) the requirement has been complied with as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person complied at the place specified in the notice`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A requirement under subsection (1) must be complied with— (a) at a place specified in the notice"
    ELSE IF `the day the person complied` AT MOST `the last day of the period specified in the notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before the end of such reasonable period as may be so specified"

-- s 947(3): the section applies only to documents and information reasonably required in connection with the Panel's functions.
-- src:13196 | (3) This section applies only to documents and information reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the Panel of its functions.
@ref s 947(3) Power to require documents and information (src:13196-13196)
GIVEN `the document or information is reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the Panel of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(3) the section applies to the document or information` MEANS
    IF `the document or information is reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the Panel of its functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only to documents and information reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the Panel of its functions."

-- s 947(4): the Panel may require a document to be authenticated, or information verified, in a manner it reasonably requires.
-- src:13197 | (4) The Panel may require—
-- src:13198 | (a) any document produced to be authenticated, or
-- src:13199 | (b) any information provided (whether in a document or otherwise) to be verified,
-- src:13200 | in such manner as it may reasonably require.
@ref s 947(4) Power to require documents and information (src:13197-13200)
GIVEN `the Panel requires a document produced to be authenticated or information provided to be verified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner is one the Panel may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(4) the Panel may require authentication or verification in that manner` MEANS
    IF `the Panel requires a document produced to be authenticated or information provided to be verified` AND `the manner is one the Panel may reasonably require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to require authentication or verification "in such manner as it may reasonably require"

-- s 947(6): a person exercising the Panel's power by authority must, if required, produce evidence of authority.
-- src:13202 | (6) A person exercising a power by virtue of subsection (5) must, if required to do so, produce evidence of his authority to exercise the power.
@ref s 947(6) Power to require documents and information (src:13202-13202)
GIVEN `the person exercises a power by virtue of subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is required to produce evidence of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(6) the person must produce evidence of authority` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person exercises a power by virtue of subsection (5)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is of "a person exercising a power by virtue of subsection (5)"
    ELSE IF `the person is required to produce evidence of authority`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, if required to do so, produce evidence of his authority"

-- s 947(7): production of a document does not affect any lien a person has on it.
-- src:13203 | (7) The production of a document in pursuance of this section does not affect any lien that a person has on the document.
@ref s 947(7) Power to require documents and information (src:13203-13203)
GIVEN `the document is produced in pursuance of section 947` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(7) the production affects a lien the person has on the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is produced in pursuance of section 947`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The production of a document in pursuance of this section does not affect any lien that a person has on the document."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of production "in pursuance of this section"

-- s 947(8): the Panel may take copies of or extracts from a document produced in pursuance of the section.
-- src:13204 | (8) The Panel may take copies of or extracts from a document produced in pursuance of this section.
@ref s 947(8) Power to require documents and information (src:13204-13204)
GIVEN `the document is produced in pursuance of section 947` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(8) the Panel may take copies of or extracts from the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is produced in pursuance of section 947`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "a document produced in pursuance of this section"

-- s 947(9): production of a document includes (a) a hard copy of information not recorded in hard copy form, (b) information in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained.
-- src:13205 | (9) A reference in this section to the production of a document includes a reference to the production of—
-- src:13206 | (a) a hard copy of information recorded otherwise than in hard copy form, or
-- src:13207 | (b) information in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained.
@ref s 947(9) Power to require documents and information (src:13205-13207)
GIVEN `the thing is a hard copy of information recorded otherwise than in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is information in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(9) the production of the thing is a production of a document` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a hard copy of information recorded otherwise than in hard copy form` OR `the thing is information in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to the production of"

-- s 947(10): a person is not required to disclose documents or information protected by legal professional privilege.
-- src:13208 | (10) A person is not required by this section to disclose documents or information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings.
@ref s 947(10) Power to require documents and information (src:13208-13208)
GIVEN `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947(10) the person is required by section 947 to disclose the document or information` MEANS
    IF `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not required by this section to disclose documents or information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption is for what a privilege claim "could be maintained" over

-- The section as a whole, for a caller: subsections (1), (3) and (10) together (the person's duty to give the Panel what it requires).
-- src:13190 | (1) The Panel may by notice in writing require a person—
-- src:13191 | (a) to produce any documents that are specified or described in the notice;
-- src:13192 | (b) to provide, in the form and manner specified in the notice, such information as may be specified or described in the notice.
-- src:13193 | (2) A requirement under subsection (1) must be complied with—
-- src:13194 | (a) at a place specified in the notice, and
-- src:13195 | (b) before the end of such reasonable period as may be so specified.
-- src:13196 | (3) This section applies only to documents and information reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the Panel of its functions.
-- src:13197 | (4) The Panel may require—
-- src:13198 | (a) any document produced to be authenticated, or
-- src:13199 | (b) any information provided (whether in a document or otherwise) to be verified,
-- src:13200 | in such manner as it may reasonably require.
-- src:13201 | (5) The Panel may authorise a person to exercise any of its powers under this section.
-- src:13202 | (6) A person exercising a power by virtue of subsection (5) must, if required to do so, produce evidence of his authority to exercise the power.
-- src:13203 | (7) The production of a document in pursuance of this section does not affect any lien that a person has on the document.
-- src:13204 | (8) The Panel may take copies of or extracts from a document produced in pursuance of this section.
-- src:13205 | (9) A reference in this section to the production of a document includes a reference to the production of—
-- src:13206 | (a) a hard copy of information recorded otherwise than in hard copy form, or
-- src:13207 | (b) information in a form from which a hard copy can be readily obtained.
-- src:13208 | (10) A person is not required by this section to disclose documents or information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings.
@ref s 947(1), (3) and (10) The person's duty to comply with the Panel's notice (src:13190-13208)
GIVEN `the Panel has required the person by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies or describes the documents, or the information and the form and manner of providing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information is reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the Panel of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 947 the person must comply with the Panel's requirement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 947(10) the person is required by section 947 to disclose the document or information` `a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not required by this section to disclose documents or information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege"
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `s 947(3) the section applies to the document or information` `the document or information is reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the Panel of its functions`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only to documents and information reasonably required in connection with the exercise by the Panel of its functions."
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `s 947(1) the Panel has required the person to produce the documents or provide the information` `the Panel has required the person by notice in writing` `the notice specifies or describes the documents, or the information and the form and manner of providing it`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Panel's power is "by notice in writing" for what the notice specifies or describes

-- s 947(1)-(2), the duty on the person with its time limit, as a regulative rule (the unit of time is a day; the period is the one the notice specifies).
DECLARE `s 947 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 947 the person required by the notice`

DECLARE `s 947 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 947 comply with the Panel's requirement at the place specified`

-- src:13190 | (1) The Panel may by notice in writing require a person—
-- src:13191 | (a) to produce any documents that are specified or described in the notice;
-- src:13192 | (b) to provide, in the form and manner specified in the notice, such information as may be specified or described in the notice.
-- src:13193 | (2) A requirement under subsection (1) must be complied with—
-- src:13194 | (a) at a place specified in the notice, and
-- src:13195 | (b) before the end of such reasonable period as may be so specified.
@ref s 947(1)-(2) The Panel's requirement and how it must be complied with (src:13190-13195)
GIVEN `the days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 947 party` `s 947 act`
`s 947(1)-(2) the person's duty to comply` MEANS
    PARTY `s 947 the person required by the notice`
    MUST `s 947 comply with the Panel's requirement at the place specified`
    WITHIN `the days the notice allows`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 947 the person required by the notice` BECAUSE "the requirement was not complied with at the place and before the end of the period the notice specifies"

-- s 948(1): the section applies to information about private affairs or a particular business, provided to the Panel.
-- src:13210 | (1) This section applies to information (in whatever form)—
-- src:13211 | (a) relating to the private affairs of an individual, or
-- src:13212 | (b) relating to any particular business,
-- src:13213 | that is provided to the Panel in connection with the exercise of its functions.
@ref s 948(1) Restrictions on disclosure (src:13210-13213)
GIVEN `the information relates to the private affairs of an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to any particular business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is provided to the Panel in connection with the exercise of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 948(1) the section applies to the information` MEANS
    IF (`the information relates to the private affairs of an individual` OR `the information relates to any particular business`)
       AND `the information is provided to the Panel in connection with the exercise of its functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section "applies to information" of the two kinds "that is provided to the Panel in connection with the exercise of its functions"

-- s 948(2): the information may not be disclosed without consent, during the individual's lifetime or while the business continues.
-- src:13214 | (2) No such information may, during the lifetime of the individual or so long as the business continues to be carried on, be disclosed without the consent of that individual or (as the case may be) the person for the time being carrying on that business.
@ref s 948(2) Restrictions on disclosure (src:13214-13214)
GIVEN `s 948(1) the section applies to the information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the private affairs of an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is still living` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to any particular business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business is still carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual (or the person for the time being carrying on the business) has consented to the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 948(2) the disclosure is prohibited` MEANS
    IF `s 948(1) the section applies to the information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF NOT (   (`the information relates to the private affairs of an individual` AND `the individual is still living`)
                 OR (`the information relates to any particular business` AND `the business is still carried on`))
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the lifetime of the individual or so long as the business continues to be carried on"
         ELSE IF `the individual (or the person for the time being carrying on the business) has consented to the disclosure`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is of disclosure "without the consent of that individual or (as the case may be) the person for the time being carrying on that business"
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No such information", that is information to which subsection (1) applies

-- s 948(3): subsection (2) does not apply to a disclosure within (a)-(d); (b)-(d) turn on Schedule 2 (coa29's), taken as seams.
-- src:13215 | (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any disclosure of information that—
-- src:13216 | (a) is made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the Panel of any of its functions,
-- src:13217 | (b) is made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 2,
-- src:13218 | (c) is of a description specified in Part 2 of that Schedule, or
-- src:13219 | (d) is made in accordance with Part 3 of that Schedule.
@ref s 948(3) Restrictions on disclosure (src:13215-13219)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the Panel of any of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 2 Part 1 the disclosure is made to a person specified in Part 1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 2 Part 2 the information is of a description specified in Part 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 2 Part 3 the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 948(3) subsection (2) does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the Panel of any of its functions`
         OR `sch 2 Part 1 the disclosure is made to a person specified in Part 1` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         OR `sch 2 Part 2 the information is of a description specified in Part 2` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         OR `sch 2 Part 3 the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF       `sch 2 Part 1 the disclosure is made to a person specified in Part 1` EQUALS NOTHING
              OR  `sch 2 Part 2 the information is of a description specified in Part 2` EQUALS NOTHING
              OR  `sch 2 Part 3 the disclosure is made in accordance with Part 3` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): limbs (b) to (d) are answered by Schedule 2 (coa29), and a limb's answer is not known
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply to any disclosure of information that— (a) is made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the Panel of any of its functions, (b) is made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 2, (c) is of a description specified in Part 2 of that Schedule, or (d) is made in accordance with Part 3 of that Schedule."

-- s 948(7): the authorities within the subsection (paragraphs (b) and (c) are blank in this text).
DECLARE `s 948(7) authority` IS ONE OF
    `s 948(7)(a) the Financial Conduct Authority`
    `s 948(7)(aa) the Prudential Regulation Authority`
    `s 948(7)(ab) the Bank of England`
    `s 948(7) another body`

-- src:13228 | (7) The authorities within this subsection are—
-- src:13229 | (a) the Financial Conduct Authority;
-- src:13230 | (aa) the Prudential Regulation Authority;
-- src:13231 | (ab) the Bank of England;
-- src:13232 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:13233 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 948(7) Restrictions on disclosure (src:13228-13233)
GIVEN body IS A `s 948(7) authority`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 948(7) the body is an authority within the subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `s 948(7)(a) the Financial Conduct Authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 948(7)(aa) the Prudential Regulation Authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 948(7)(ab) the Bank of England` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 948(7) another body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The authorities within this subsection are" the three named, with paragraphs (b) and (c) shown blank, and no "only" (marginal reading, NOTES.md)

-- s 948(6): subsection (2) does not apply to (a) a disclosure by an authority within (7) of what the Panel disclosed to it in reliance on (3), (b) a disclosure of such information by anyone who got it from such an authority.
-- src:13225 | (6) Subsection (2) does not apply to—
-- src:13226 | (a) the disclosure by an authority within subsection (7) of information disclosed to it by the Panel in reliance on subsection (3);
-- src:13227 | (b) the disclosure of such information by anyone who has obtained it directly or indirectly from an authority within subsection (7).
@ref s 948(6) Restrictions on disclosure (src:13225-13227)
GIVEN `s 948(7) the discloser is an authority within subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the information was disclosed to the authority by the Panel in reliance on subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the discloser obtained the information directly or indirectly from an authority within subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 948(6) subsection (2) does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    IF (`s 948(7) the discloser is an authority within subsection (7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the information was disclosed to the authority by the Panel in reliance on subsection (3)`) OR `the discloser obtained the information directly or indirectly from an authority within subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `s 948(7) the discloser is an authority within subsection (7)` EQUALS NOTHING AND `the information was disclosed to the authority by the Panel in reliance on subsection (3)`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): whether the discloser is one of the authorities within subsection (7) is not shown
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply to— (a) the disclosure by an authority within subsection (7) of information disclosed to it by the Panel in reliance on subsection (3); (b) the disclosure of such information by anyone who has obtained it directly or indirectly from an authority within subsection (7)."

-- s 948(8): the section does not prohibit disclosure of information that is or has been available to the public from another source.
-- src:13234 | (8) This section does not prohibit the disclosure of information if the information is or has been available to the public from any other source.
@ref s 948(8) Restrictions on disclosure (src:13234-13234)
GIVEN `the information is or has been available to the public from any other source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 948(8) the section prohibits the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the information is or has been available to the public from any other source`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not prohibit the disclosure of information if the information is or has been available to the public from any other source."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of information "available to the public from any other source"

-- s 948(9): nothing in the section authorises a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation.
-- src:13235 | (9) Nothing in this section authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation.
@ref s 948(9) Restrictions on disclosure (src:13235-13235)
GIVEN `the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 948(9) the section authorises the disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the disclosure would contravene the data protection legislation`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section authorises the making of a disclosure in contravention of the data protection legislation."
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what the section does not authorise, not what it does
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the data protection legislation" is defined in section 1173(1) by the Data Protection Act 2018, outside the sources

-- The section as a whole, for a caller: subsections (2), (3), (6) and (8) put together (each is a separate answer above).
-- src:13214 | (2) No such information may, during the lifetime of the individual or so long as the business continues to be carried on, be disclosed without the consent of that individual or (as the case may be) the person for the time being carrying on that business.
-- src:13215 | (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to any disclosure of information that—
-- src:13216 | (a) is made for the purpose of facilitating the carrying out by the Panel of any of its functions,
-- src:13217 | (b) is made to a person specified in Part 1 of Schedule 2,
-- src:13218 | (c) is of a description specified in Part 2 of that Schedule, or
-- src:13219 | (d) is made in accordance with Part 3 of that Schedule.
-- src:13220 | (4) The Secretary of State may amend Schedule 2 by order subject to negative resolution procedure.
-- src:13221 | (5) An order under subsection (4) must not—
-- src:13222 | (a) amend Part 1 of Schedule 2 by specifying a person unless the person exercises functions of a public nature (whether or not he exercises any other function);
-- src:13223 | (b) amend Part 2 of Schedule 2 by adding or modifying a description of disclosure unless the purpose for which the disclosure is permitted is likely to facilitate the exercise of a function of a public nature;
-- src:13224 | (c) amend Part 3 of Schedule 2 so as to have the effect of permitting disclosures to be made to a body other than one that exercises functions of a public nature in a country or territory outside the United Kingdom.
-- src:13225 | (6) Subsection (2) does not apply to—
-- src:13226 | (a) the disclosure by an authority within subsection (7) of information disclosed to it by the Panel in reliance on subsection (3);
-- src:13227 | (b) the disclosure of such information by anyone who has obtained it directly or indirectly from an authority within subsection (7).
-- src:13228 | (7) The authorities within this subsection are—
-- src:13229 | (a) the Financial Conduct Authority;
-- src:13230 | (aa) the Prudential Regulation Authority;
-- src:13231 | (ab) the Bank of England;
-- src:13232 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:13233 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:13234 | (8) This section does not prohibit the disclosure of information if the information is or has been available to the public from any other source.
@ref s 948(2), (3), (6) and (8) The restriction on disclosure and its exceptions (src:13214-13234)
GIVEN `the answer under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (6)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 948 the disclosure is prohibited by section 948` MEANS
    IF `the answer under subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer under subsection (6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (2) does not apply to"
    ELSE IF `the answer under subsection (8)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not prohibit the disclosure of information if the information is or has been available to the public from any other source."
         ELSE IF `the answer under subsection (3)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the answer under subsection (6)` EQUALS NOTHING
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an exception in subsection (3) or (6) applies turns on Schedule 2 or on subsection (7), and the answer is not known
              ELSE `the answer under subsection (2)`

-- s 949(1): the offence of disclosure in contravention of section 948, unless the person did not know or took all reasonable steps.
-- src:13237 | (1) A person who discloses information in contravention of section 948 is guilty of an offence, unless—
-- src:13238 | (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided as mentioned in section 948(1), or
-- src:13239 | (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence.
@ref s 949(1) Offence of disclosure in contravention of section 948 (src:13237-13239)
GIVEN `s 948 the disclosure is in contravention of section 948` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided as mentioned in section 948(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 949(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 948 the disclosure is in contravention of section 948`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided as mentioned in section 948(1)`
           OR `the person took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is guilty of an offence, unless— (a) he did not know, and had no reason to suspect, that the information had been provided as mentioned in section 948(1), or (b) he took all reasonable steps and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of a person "who discloses information in contravention of section 948"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the disclosure contravenes section 948 depends on Schedule 2 and the data protection legislation

-- s 949(2): the penalty, by where the person is convicted.
-- src:13241 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
@ref s 949(2)(a) Offence of disclosure in contravention of section 948 (src:13241-13241)
`s 949(2)(a) the penalty on conviction on indictment` MEANS
    -- how convicted, imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding, daily default fine, imprisonment and fine together
    Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE

-- src:13243 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
@ref s 949(2)(b)(i) Offence of disclosure in contravention of section 948 (src:13243-13243)
`s 949(2)(b)(i) the penalty on summary conviction in England and Wales` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE

-- src:13244 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 949(2)(b)(ii) Offence of disclosure in contravention of section 948 (src:13244-13244)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 949(2)(b)(ii) the penalty on summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland` MEANS
    Penalty OF `how convicted`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE

-- src:13240 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:13241 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:13242 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:13243 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:13244 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 949(2) Offence of disclosure in contravention of section 948 (src:13240-13244)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 949(2) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST `s 949(2)(a) the penalty on conviction on indictment`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST `s 949(2)(b)(i) the penalty on summary conviction in England and Wales`
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (`s 949(2)(b)(ii) the penalty on summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland` `on summary conviction in Scotland`)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (`s 949(2)(b)(ii) the penalty on summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland` `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives one penalty for England and Wales and another for Scotland or Northern Ireland, so a conviction not placed is not covered

-- s 949(3): where a company or other body corporate commits the offence, every officer in default also commits it.
-- src:13245 | (3) Where a company or other body corporate commits an offence under this section, an offence is also committed by every officer of the company or other body corporate who is in default.
@ref s 949(3) Offence of disclosure in contravention of section 948 (src:13245-13245)
GIVEN `the company or other body corporate commits an offence under section 949` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 949(3) the officer also commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company or other body corporate commits an offence under section 949` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the company or other body corporate commits an offence under section 949` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body committed the offence, or the officer is "in default", is answered elsewhere (section 949(1), section 1121)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is "also committed by every officer of the company or other body corporate who is in default"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Co-operation, hearings and appeals (ss 950 and 951)`

-- s 950(1): the Panel's duty to take steps to co-operate with the named bodies.
DECLARE `s 950(1) body` IS ONE OF
    `s 950(1)(a) the Financial Conduct Authority`
    `s 950(1)(aa) the Prudential Regulation Authority`
    `s 950(1)(ab) the Bank of England`
    `s 950(1)(c) a person or body outside the United Kingdom exercising similar functions`
    `s 950(1) another body`

-- src:13248 | (1) The Panel must take such steps as it considers appropriate to co-operate with—
-- src:13249 | (a) the Financial Conduct Authority;
-- src:13250 | (aa) the Prudential Regulation Authority;
-- src:13251 | (ab) the Bank of England;
-- src:13252 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:13253 | (c) any other person or body that exercises functions of a public nature, under legislation in any country or territory outside the United Kingdom, that appear to the Panel to be similar to its own functions or those of the Financial Conduct Authority or the Prudential Regulation Authority or similar to the regulatory functions of the Bank of England.
@ref s 950(1) Panel's duty of co-operation (src:13248-13253)
GIVEN body IS A `s 950(1) body`
      `the body exercises functions of a public nature under legislation in a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the functions appear to the Panel to be similar to its own or to those of the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 950(1) the Panel must take steps to co-operate with the body` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `s 950(1)(a) the Financial Conduct Authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 950(1)(aa) the Prudential Regulation Authority` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 950(1)(ab) the Bank of England` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 950(1)(c) a person or body outside the United Kingdom exercising similar functions` THEN
        IF `the body exercises functions of a public nature under legislation in a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` AND `the functions appear to the Panel to be similar to its own or to those of the Financial Conduct Authority, the Prudential Regulation Authority or the Bank of England`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) is a body with functions of a public nature, under legislation outside the United Kingdom, that "appear to the Panel to be similar"
    WHEN `s 950(1) another body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the duty is to co-operate with the bodies listed, and paragraph (b) is blank in this text

-- s 950(2): co-operation may include sharing information the Panel is not prevented from disclosing.
-- src:13254 | (2) Co-operation may include the sharing of information that the Panel is not prevented from disclosing.
@ref s 950(2) Panel's duty of co-operation (src:13254-13254)
GIVEN `the thing is the sharing of information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Panel is not prevented from disclosing the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 950(2) the thing is a form of co-operation` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the sharing of information` AND `the Panel is not prevented from disclosing the information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "Co-operation may include the sharing of information that the Panel is not prevented from disclosing."

-- s 951(1): a person affected by a decision of the Panel may have it reviewed by the Hearings Committee, as the rules specify.
-- src:13257 | (1) Rules must provide for a decision of the Panel to be subject to review by a committee of the Panel (the “Hearings Committee”) at the instance of such persons affected by the decision as are specified in the rules.
@ref s 951(1) Hearings and appeals (src:13257-13257)
GIVEN `the person is affected by the decision of the Panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 943 the rules specify the person as one who may have the decision reviewed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 951(1) the person may have the Panel's decision reviewed by the Hearings Committee` MEANS
    IF `the person is affected by the decision of the Panel` AND `s 943 the rules specify the person as one who may have the decision reviewed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): review is "at the instance of such persons affected by the decision as are specified in the rules", and the rules are not among the sources

-- s 951(3): a right of appeal against a decision of the Hearings Committee to the Takeover Appeal Board, as the rules specify.
-- src:13259 | (3) Rules must provide for there to be a right of appeal against a decision of the Hearings Committee to an independent tribunal (the “Takeover Appeal Board”) in such circumstances and subject to such conditions as are specified in the rules.
@ref s 951(3) Hearings and appeals (src:13259-13259)
GIVEN `the decision is a decision of the Hearings Committee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 943 the rules give a right of appeal in these circumstances and subject to these conditions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 951(3) the person has a right of appeal to the Takeover Appeal Board` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a decision of the Hearings Committee` AND `s 943 the rules give a right of appeal in these circumstances and subject to these conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the conditions are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the right of appeal is "in such circumstances and subject to such conditions as are specified in the rules", and the rules are not among the sources

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Contravention of rules etc (ss 952 to 956)`

-- s 952(1): rules may confer power on the Panel to impose sanctions on a person who acted in breach of rules or failed to comply with a direction.
-- src:13271 | (1) Rules may contain provision conferring power on the Panel to impose sanctions on a person who has—
-- src:13272 | (a) acted in breach of rules, or
-- src:13273 | (b) failed to comply with a direction given by virtue of section 946.
@ref s 952(1) Sanctions (src:13271-13273)
GIVEN `s 943 the rules confer power on the Panel to impose the sanction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has acted in breach of rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has failed to comply with a direction given by virtue of section 946` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 952(1) the Panel may impose the sanction on the person` MEANS
    IF `s 943 the rules confer power on the Panel to impose the sanction` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`the person has acted in breach of rules` OR `the person has failed to comply with a direction given by virtue of section 946`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the power exists only if "rules made by virtue of subsection (1) confer power", and the rules are not among the sources

-- s 952(2): subsection (3) applies where the rules confer power to impose a sanction of a kind the City Code did not provide for.
-- src:13274 | (2) Subsection (3) applies where rules made by virtue of subsection (1) confer power on the Panel to impose a sanction of a kind not provided for by the City Code on Takeovers and Mergers as it had effect immediately before the passing of this Act.
@ref s 952(2) Sanctions (src:13274-13274)
GIVEN `rules made by virtue of subsection (1) confer power on the Panel to impose the sanction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanction is of a kind not provided for by the City Code on Takeovers and Mergers as it had effect immediately before the passing of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 952(2) subsection (3) applies` MEANS
    IF `rules made by virtue of subsection (1) confer power on the Panel to impose the sanction` AND `the sanction is of a kind not provided for by the City Code on Takeovers and Mergers as it had effect immediately before the passing of this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3) applies where rules made by virtue of subsection (1) confer power on the Panel to impose a sanction of a kind not provided for by the City Code on Takeovers and Mergers as it had effect immediately before the passing of this Act."

-- s 952(3): the Panel must prepare a policy statement; an element must be that it has regard to the factors in (4).
-- src:13275 | (3) The Panel must prepare a statement (a “policy statement”) of its policy with respect to—
