      `the sanction is in the nature of a financial penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement sets out the policy on the amount of the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an element of the policy is that the Panel has regard to the factors in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 952(3) the policy statement is the statement the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 952(2) subsection (3) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises only in a case to which subsection (2) brings it
    ELSE IF       `the statement sets out the policy on the imposition of the sanction`
              AND ((NOT (`the sanction is in the nature of a financial penalty`)) OR `the statement sets out the policy on the amount of the penalty`)
              AND `an element of the policy is that the Panel has regard to the factors in subsection (4)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Panel must prepare a statement (a “policy statement”) of its policy with respect to— (a) the imposition of the sanction in question, and (b) where the sanction is in the nature of a financial penalty, the amount of the penalty that may be imposed."

-- s 952(4): the factors the Panel has regard to.
DECLARE `s 952(4) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 952(4)(a) the seriousness of the breach or failure in relation to the nature of the rule or direction contravened`
    `s 952(4)(b) the extent to which the breach or failure was deliberate or reckless`
    `s 952(4)(c) whether the person on whom the sanction is to be imposed is an individual`
    `s 952(4) another matter`

-- src:13279 | (4) The factors are—
-- src:13280 | (a) the seriousness of the breach or failure in question in relation to the nature of the rule or direction contravened;
-- src:13281 | (b) the extent to which the breach or failure was deliberate or reckless;
-- src:13282 | (c) whether the person on whom the sanction is to be imposed is an individual.
@ref s 952(4) Sanctions (src:13279-13282)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 952(4) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 952(4) the matter is one of the factors` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 952(4)(a) the seriousness of the breach or failure in relation to the nature of the rule or direction contravened` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 952(4)(b) the extent to which the breach or failure was deliberate or reckless` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 952(4)(c) whether the person on whom the sanction is to be imposed is an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 952(4) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The factors are" the three listed, with no "only"

