-- s 953(1): the section applies where a takeover bid is made for a company with securities admitted to trading on a UK regulated market.
-- src:13288 | (1) This section applies where a takeover bid is made for a company that has securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 953(1) Failure to comply with rules about bid documentation (src:13288-13288)
GIVEN `sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has securities carrying voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1173(1) the securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the market is in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 953(1) the section applies to the bid` MEANS
    IF `sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 1173(1) the securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "takeover bid" is paragraph 20(1) of Schedule 1C and "regulated market" is Article 2.1.13 of Regulation (EU) No. 600/2014 (section 1173(1))
    ELSE IF       `sch 1C para 20(1) the offer is a takeover bid` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `the company has securities carrying voting rights`
              AND `s 1173(1) the securities are admitted to trading on a regulated market` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `the market is in the United Kingdom`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a takeover bid is made for a company that has securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market in the United Kingdom."

-- s 953(2): an offence where an offer document does not comply with the offer document rules, by (a) the person making the bid, (b) any director, officer or member of a body making the bid who caused publication.
-- src:13289 | (2) Where an offer document published in respect of the bid does not comply with offer document rules, an offence is committed by—
-- src:13290 | (a) the person making the bid, and
-- src:13291 | (b) where the person making the bid is a body of persons, any director, officer or member of that body who caused the document to be published.
@ref s 953(2) Failure to comply with rules about bid documentation (src:13289-13291)
GIVEN `s 953(1) the section applies to the bid` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offer document published in respect of the bid does not comply with the offer document rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person making the bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the bid is a body of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director, officer or member of that body who caused the document to be published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 953(2) an offence is committed by the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 953(1) the section applies to the bid`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a takeover bid is made for a company that has securities carrying voting rights admitted to trading on a regulated market in the United Kingdom."
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies depends on Schedule 1C paragraph 20(1) and on "regulated market" (section 1173(1))
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF       `the offer document published in respect of the bid does not comply with the offer document rules`
             AND (   `the person is the person making the bid`
                  OR (`the person making the bid is a body of persons` AND `the person is a director, officer or member of that body who caused the document to be published`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is committed by "(a) the person making the bid, and (b) where the person making the bid is a body of persons, any director, officer or member of that body who caused the document to be published"

