-- s 953(5): where the offence is committed by a company or other body corporate, the references to a director, officer or member extend to those of the relevant body.
DECLARE `s 953(5) provision extended` IS ONE OF
    `s 953(5)(a) subsection (2)(b)`
    `s 953(5)(b) subsection (4)`

-- src:13298 | (5) Where an offence is committed under subsection (2)(b) or (4) by a company or other body corporate (“the relevant body”)—
-- src:13299 | (a) subsection (2)(b) has effect as if the reference to a director, officer or member of the person making the bid included a reference to a director, officer or member of the relevant body;
-- src:13300 | (b) subsection (4) has effect as if the reference to a director or other officer of the company referred to in subsection (1) included a reference to a director, officer or member of the relevant body.
@ref s 953(5) Failure to comply with rules about bid documentation (src:13298-13300)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 953(5) provision extended`
      `an offence is committed under subsection (2)(b) or (4) by a company or other body corporate (the relevant body)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director, officer or member of the relevant body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 953(5) the person is within the provision as extended` MEANS
    IF `an offence is committed under subsection (2)(b) or (4) by a company or other body corporate (the relevant body)` AND `the person is a director, officer or member of the relevant body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the extension is "where an offence is committed under subsection (2)(b) or (4) by a company or other body corporate"
    -- limb (a) extends subsection (2)(b) and limb (b) extends subsection (4); both extend to a director, officer or member of the relevant body, so the answer does not turn on which provision is named

-- s 953(6): the penalty for the offence.
-- src:13301 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:13302 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:13303 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 953(6) Failure to comply with rules about bid documentation (src:13301-13303)
GIVEN `how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 953(6) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

