    IF `s 943 the rules confer power on the Panel to order the compensation` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person is in breach of a rule the effect of which is to require the payment of money`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the amount is "such compensation as it thinks just and reasonable": the Panel's judgment, not a number in the text
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the power exists only if "rules may confer power", and the rules are not among the sources

-- s 955(2): "the court" in section 955 is the High Court or, in Scotland, the Court of Session.
DECLARE `s 955(2) court` IS ONE OF
    `s 955(2) the High Court`
    `s 955(2) the Court of Session`

-- src:13323 | (2) In subsection (1) “the court” means the High Court or, in Scotland, the Court of Session.
@ref s 955(2) Enforcement by the court (src:13323-13323)
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A `s 955(2) court`
`s 955(2) the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN `s 955(2) the High Court`
    WHEN `Scotland` THEN `s 955(2) the Court of Session`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `s 955(2) the High Court`

-- s 955(4): definitions of "contravene", "disclosure requirement" and "rule-based requirement".
-- src:13329 | “contravene” includes fail to comply;
@ref s 955(4)“contravene” Enforcement by the court (src:13329-13329)
GIVEN `the thing is a failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 955(4) the thing is a contravention` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a failure to comply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“contravene” includes fail to comply"

-- src:13330 | “disclosure requirement” means a requirement imposed under section 947;
@ref s 955(4)“disclosure requirement” Enforcement by the court (src:13330-13330)
GIVEN `the requirement is imposed under section 947` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 955(4) the requirement is a disclosure requirement` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is imposed under section 947`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“disclosure requirement” means a requirement imposed under section 947"

-- src:13331 | “rule-based requirement” means a requirement imposed by or under rules.
@ref s 955(4)“rule-based requirement” Enforcement by the court (src:13331-13331)
GIVEN `the requirement is imposed by or under rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 955(4) the requirement is a rule-based requirement` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is imposed by or under rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“rule-based requirement” means a requirement imposed by or under rules"

-- s 955(1): on the Panel's application the court may make any order it thinks fit to secure compliance.
-- src:13319 | (1) If, on the application of the Panel, the court is satisfied—
-- src:13320 | (a) that there is a reasonable likelihood that a person will contravene a rule-based requirement, or
-- src:13321 | (b) that a person has contravened a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement,
-- src:13322 | the court may make any order it thinks fit to secure compliance with the requirement.
@ref s 955(1) Enforcement by the court (src:13319-13322)
GIVEN `the Panel has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable likelihood that the person will contravene a rule-based requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has contravened a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 955(1) the court may make an order against the person to secure compliance` MEANS
    IF `the Panel has applied to the court` AND (`the court is satisfied that there is a reasonable likelihood that the person will contravene a rule-based requirement` OR `the court is satisfied that the person has contravened a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "on the application of the Panel" where the court is satisfied of (a) or (b)

-- s 955(3): except as provided by (1), no person has a right to seek an injunction (or, in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to prevent a contravention.
-- src:13324 | (3) Except as provided by subsection (1), no person—
-- src:13325 | (a) has a right to seek an injunction, or
-- src:13326 | (b) in Scotland, has title or interest to seek an interdict or an order for specific performance,
-- src:13327 | to prevent a person from contravening (or continuing to contravene) a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement.
@ref s 955(3) Enforcement by the court (src:13324-13327)
GIVEN `the remedy (an injunction or, in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) is sought under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the remedy is sought to prevent a person from contravening (or continuing to contravene) a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 955(3) the person has a right to seek the remedy` MEANS
    IF `the remedy (an injunction or, in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) is sought under subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is "Except as provided by subsection (1)", and subsection (1) is the Panel's application
    ELSE IF `the remedy is sought to prevent a person from contravening (or continuing to contravene) a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as provided by subsection (1), no person— (a) has a right to seek an injunction, or (b) in Scotland, has title or interest to seek an interdict or an order for specific performance"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on seeking a remedy "to prevent a person from contravening (or continuing to contravene) a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement"

-- s 956(1): contravention of a rule-based or disclosure requirement gives no right of action for breach of statutory duty.
-- src:13333 | (1) Contravention of a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement does not give rise to any right of action for breach of statutory duty.
@ref s 956(1) No action for breach of statutory duty etc (src:13333-13333)
GIVEN `the contravention is of a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 956(1) the contravention gives rise to a right of action for breach of statutory duty` MEANS
    IF `the contravention is of a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Contravention of a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement does not give rise to any right of action for breach of statutory duty."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a rule-based requirement or a disclosure requirement"

-- s 956(2): contravention of a rule-based requirement does not make a transaction void or unenforceable, or (subject to the rules) affect the validity of any other thing.
-- src:13334 | (2) Contravention of a rule-based requirement does not make any transaction void or unenforceable or (subject to any provision made by rules) affect the validity of any other thing.
@ref s 956(2) No action for breach of statutory duty etc (src:13334-13334)
GIVEN `the contravention is of a rule-based requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 943 the rules make provision about the validity of the thing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 956(2) the contravention makes the thing void or unenforceable or affects its validity` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the contravention is of a rule-based requirement`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "Contravention of a rule-based requirement"
    ELSE IF `the thing is a transaction`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Contravention of a rule-based requirement does not make any transaction void or unenforceable"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 943 the rules make provision about the validity of the thing`
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or (subject to any provision made by rules) affect the validity of any other thing"
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any provision made by rules", and the rules are not among the sources
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the rules make provision is not known

-- s 956(3): "contravention" includes failure to comply; the other two terms mean what section 955 gives them.
-- src:13336 | (a) “contravention” includes failure to comply;
@ref s 956(3)(a) No action for breach of statutory duty etc (src:13336-13336)
GIVEN `the thing is a failure to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 956(3)(a) the thing is a contravention` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a failure to comply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“contravention” includes failure to comply"

-- src:13337 | (b) “disclosure requirement” and “rule-based requirement” have the same meaning as in section 955.
@ref s 956(3)(b) No action for breach of statutory duty etc (src:13337-13337)
GIVEN `the requirement has the meaning section 955 gives it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 956(3)(b) the term has the same meaning as in section 955` MEANS
    IF `the requirement has the meaning section 955 gives it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“disclosure requirement” and “rule-based requirement” have the same meaning as in section 955"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Funding and miscellaneous (ss 957 to 963)`

-- s 957(1): rules may provide for fees or charges to be payable to the Panel to meet its expenses.
-- src:13340 | (1) Rules may provide for fees or charges to be payable to the Panel for the purpose of meeting any part of its expenses.
@ref s 957(1) Fees and charges (src:13340-13340)
GIVEN `s 943 the rules provide for the fee or charge to be payable to the Panel` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 957(1) the fee or charge is payable to the Panel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 943 the rules provide for the fee or charge to be payable to the Panel`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the fee is payable only "Rules may provide"; the text does not say what follows when the rules do not
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what the Panel's rules provide is not among the sources

-- s 957(2): "expenses of the Panel" are any expenses incurred in connection with the discharge of its functions, including in particular (a) to (c).
-- src:13341 | (2) A reference in this section or section 958 to expenses of the Panel is to any expenses that have been or are to be incurred by the Panel in, or in connection with, the discharge of its functions, including in particular—
-- src:13342 | (a) payments in respect of the expenses of the Takeover Appeal Board;
-- src:13343 | (b) the cost of repaying the principal of, and of paying any interest on, any money borrowed by the Panel;
-- src:13344 | (c) the cost of maintaining adequate reserves.
@ref s 957(2) Fees and charges (src:13341-13344)
GIVEN `the expense has been or is to be incurred by the Panel in, or in connection with, the discharge of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 957(2) the expense is an expense of the Panel` MEANS
    IF `the expense has been or is to be incurred by the Panel in, or in connection with, the discharge of its functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- including the expenses of the Takeover Appeal Board, the cost of repaying and paying interest on money borrowed, the cost of maintaining adequate reserves
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A reference in this section or section 958 to expenses of the Panel is to any expenses that have been or are to be incurred by the Panel in, or in connection with, the discharge of its functions"

-- s 958(2): the levy is payable only by persons or bodies that appear to the Secretary of State to be capable of being directly affected or to have a substantial interest.
-- src:13350 | (2) The power to specify (or to specify descriptions of) persons or bodies must be exercised in such a way that the levy is payable only by persons or bodies that appear to the Secretary of State—
-- src:13351 | (a) to be capable of being directly affected by the exercise of any of the functions of the Panel, or
-- src:13352 | (b) otherwise to have a substantial interest in the exercise of any of those functions.
@ref s 958(2) Levy (src:13350-13352)
GIVEN `the person or body appears to the Secretary of State to be capable of being directly affected by the exercise of any of the functions of the Panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or body appears to the Secretary of State otherwise to have a substantial interest in the exercise of any of those functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 958(2) the levy may be made payable by the person or body` MEANS
    IF `the person or body appears to the Secretary of State to be capable of being directly affected by the exercise of any of the functions of the Panel` OR `the person or body appears to the Secretary of State otherwise to have a substantial interest in the exercise of any of those functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the levy is payable only by persons or bodies that appear to the Secretary of State"

-- s 959: an amount payable by virtue of section 957 or 958 is a debt due to the Panel and is recoverable accordingly.
-- src:13370 | 959 Recovery of fees, charges or levy
-- src:13371 | An amount payable by any person or body by virtue of section 957 or 958 is a debt due from that person or body to the Panel, and is recoverable accordingly.
@ref s 959 Recovery of fees, charges or levy (src:13370-13371)
GIVEN `s 957(1) the amount is payable by virtue of section 957` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 958 the amount is payable by virtue of section 958 (regulations under it provide for the levy)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 959 the amount is a debt due to the Panel` MEANS
    IF `s 957(1) the amount is payable by virtue of section 957` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 958 the amount is payable by virtue of section 958 (regulations under it provide for the levy)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the debt is of "An amount payable by any person or body by virtue of section 957 or 958"

-- s 960: the Panel, though an unincorporated body, can bring or defend proceedings in its own name.
DECLARE `s 960 proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `s 960(a) proceedings under Chapter 1 brought by the Panel`
    `s 960(b) any other proceedings brought or defended by the Panel`
    `s 960 proceedings of another kind`

-- src:13373 | 960 Panel as party to proceedings
-- src:13374 | The Panel is capable (despite being an unincorporated body) of—
-- src:13375 | (a) bringing proceedings under this Chapter in its own name;
-- src:13376 | (b) bringing or defending any other proceedings in its own name.
@ref s 960 Panel as party to proceedings (src:13373-13376)
GIVEN proceedings IS A `s 960 proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 960 the Panel is capable of the proceedings in its own name` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceedings
    WHEN `s 960(a) proceedings under Chapter 1 brought by the Panel` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 960(b) any other proceedings brought or defended by the Panel` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 960 proceedings of another kind` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section lists the Panel's capacity to bring proceedings under the Chapter and to bring or defend any other proceedings

-- s 961(1)-(3): neither the Panel nor anyone within (2) is liable in damages for anything done in discharging its functions, except in bad faith or where the Human Rights Act 1998 s 6(1) applies.
-- src:13379 | (2) A person is within this subsection if—
-- src:13380 | (a) he is (or is acting as) a member, officer or member of staff of the Panel, or
-- src:13381 | (b) he is a person authorised under section 947(5).
@ref s 961(2) Exemption from liability in damages (src:13379-13381)
GIVEN `the person is (or is acting as) a member, officer or member of staff of the Panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised under section 947(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 961(2) the person is within the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the person is (or is acting as) a member, officer or member of staff of the Panel` OR `the person is authorised under section 947(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person is within this subsection if" he is within (a) or (b)

-- src:13378 | (1) Neither the Panel, nor any person within subsection (2), is to be liable in damages for anything done (or omitted to be done) in, or in connection with, the discharge or purported discharge of the Panel's functions.
@ref s 961(1) Exemption from liability in damages (src:13378-13378)
GIVEN `the defendant is the Panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 961(2) the person is within the subsection` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing was done (or omitted) in, or in connection with, the discharge or purported discharge of the Panel's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 961(3)(a) the act or omission is shown to have been in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 961(3)(b) damages are claimed on the ground that the act or omission was unlawful as a result of section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 961(1) the defendant is liable in damages` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the defendant is the Panel` OR (`s 961(2) the person is within the subsection` EQUALS JUST TRUE))) OR (NOT (`the thing was done (or omitted) in, or in connection with, the discharge or purported discharge of the Panel's functions`))
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption is of "the Panel, [and] any person within subsection (2)" for "anything done (or omitted to be done) in, or in connection with, the discharge or purported discharge of the Panel's functions"
    ELSE IF `s 961(3)(a) the act or omission is shown to have been in bad faith` OR `s 961(3)(b) damages are claimed on the ground that the act or omission was unlawful as a result of section 6(1) of the Human Rights Act 1998`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply" in the two cases, and the text does not say that liability follows
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Neither the Panel, nor any person within subsection (2), is to be liable in damages for anything done (or omitted to be done) in, or in connection with, the discharge or purported discharge of the Panel's functions."

-- s 962: a statement made in response to a requirement under section 947(1), or a court order under section 955 to secure compliance with it, may not be used against him in criminal proceedings, except for the perjury offences listed.
DECLARE `s 962(2) offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 962(2)(a) an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911`
    `s 962(2)(b) an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995`
    `s 962(2)(c) an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979`
    `s 962(2) any other offence`

-- src:13386 | (1) A statement made by a person in response to—
-- src:13387 | (a) a requirement under section 947(1), or
-- src:13388 | (b) an order made by the court under section 955 to secure compliance with such a requirement,
-- src:13389 | may not be used against him in criminal proceedings in which he is charged with an offence to which this subsection applies.
-- src:13390 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than an offence under one of the following provisions (which concern false statements made otherwise than on oath)—
-- src:13391 | (a) section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911 (c. 6);
-- src:13392 | (b) section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995 (c. 39);
-- src:13393 | (c) Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (S.I. 1979/1714 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 962(1)-(2) Privilege against self-incrimination (src:13386-13393)
GIVEN `the statement was made in response to a requirement under section 947(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement was made in response to an order of the court under section 955 to secure compliance with such a requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `s 962(2) offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 962(1) the statement may be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the statement was made in response to a requirement under section 947(1)` OR `the statement was made in response to an order of the court under section 955 to secure compliance with such a requirement`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "A statement made by a person in response to" a section 947(1) requirement or a section 955 order
    ELSE CONSIDER offence
         WHEN `s 962(2)(a) an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) "applies to any offence other than" the three perjury offences, so it says nothing about them
         WHEN `s 962(2)(b) an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): as for paragraph (a)
         WHEN `s 962(2)(c) an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): as for paragraph (a)
         WHEN `s 962(2) any other offence` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be used against him in criminal proceedings in which he is charged with an offence to which this subsection applies"

-- s 963(1): after the end of each financial year the Panel must publish a report.
-- src:13395 | (1) After the end of each financial year the Panel must publish a report.
@ref s 963(1) Annual reports (src:13395-13395)
