      `the report includes the Panel's accounts for that year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report mentions the matters the Panel considers to be of relevance to the discharge of its functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 963(2) the report has the content the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the report sets out how the Panel's functions were discharged in the year` AND `the report includes the Panel's accounts for that year` AND `the report mentions the matters the Panel considers to be of relevance to the discharge of its functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must— (a) set out how the Panel's functions were discharged in the year in question; (b) include the Panel's accounts for that year; (c) mention any matters the Panel considers to be of relevance to the discharge of its functions."
